### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### Team authorization — org admin ▸ team admin ▸ member
###
### Schema:
###   team  view   = admin + member + organization->manage
###         manage = admin + organization->manage
###
### Actors (org "teamflowco"):
###   • Fran — founder ⇒ ORG admin
###   • Adam — promoted to TEAM admin of Dev (by Fran, the org admin)
###   • Otto — plain member of Dev (added by Adam, the team admin)
###
### Rules verified:
###   • only org admin creates teams           (Adam create → 403, Fran → 201)
###   • org admin makes a user team admin       (Fran promote Adam → 204)
###   • team admin CAN add members              (Adam add Otto → 201)
###   • only ORG admin can promote to admin     (Adam promote Otto → 403)
###   • member cannot manage                    (Otto add/members/delete → 403)
###   • view: admin, member, org admin          (all GET → 200)
###   • members list needs manage               (Fran/Adam → 200, Otto → 403)
###
### Self-contained. Run top-to-bottom. Requires the app up with
### orgcraft.spicedb.enabled=true and SpiceDB reachable — with SpiceDB
### disabled the permit-all fallback lets every check pass, so the 403s
### won't happen and the assertions become meaningless.
### NOTE: SpiceDB tuples are written by async module-event listeners, so
###       let each write settle before the verifying read (top-to-bottom
###       manual execution is plenty).
### NOTE: team-member endpoints live under /api/teams (no /v1), while team
###       CRUD lives under /api/v1/teams.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@slug = teamflowco
@franEmail = fran@teamflowco.com
@pwd = Password@123
@adamEmail = adam@teamflowco.com
@ottoEmail = otto@teamflowco.com

### T1. Register org (public) → Fran becomes ORG admin
POST {{host}}/api/v1/organizations
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "TeamFlowCo",
  "slug": "{{slug}}",
  "founderFirstName": "Fran",
  "founderLastName": "Founder",
  "founderEmail": "{{franEmail}}",
  "founderPassword": "{{pwd}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("orgId", response.body.organizationId);
    client.log("orgId=" + response.body.organizationId);
%}

### T2. Login as Fran (org admin)
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{franEmail}}&password={{pwd}}&tenant={{slug}}

### T3. Fran creates Adam (future team admin)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Adam", "lastName": "Admin", "email": "{{adamEmail}}", "password": "{{pwd}}" }

> {% client.global.set("adamId", response.body.id); %}

### T4. Fran creates Otto (future member)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "firstName": "Otto", "lastName": "Member", "email": "{{ottoEmail}}", "password": "{{pwd}}" }

> {% client.global.set("ottoId", response.body.id); %}

### T5. Fran (org admin) creates team Dev → 201
POST {{host}}/api/v1/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Dev Team" }

> {%
    client.test("Org admin creates team", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201, "expected 201, got " + response.status); });
    client.global.set("teamId", response.body.id);
    client.log("teamId=" + response.body.id);
%}

### T6. Fran adds Adam as member of Dev → 201 (org admin can add members)
POST {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamId": "{{teamId}}", "userId": "{{adamId}}" }

> {% client.test("Org admin adds Adam", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201, "expected 201, got " + response.status); }); %}

### T7. Fran promotes Adam to TEAM admin → 204 (only org admin may promote)
PUT {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members/{{adamId}}/admin

> {% client.test("Org admin promotes Adam to team admin", function () { client.assert(response.status === 204, "expected 204, got " + response.status); }); %}

### T8. Fran lists teams → sees Dev via organization->manage (1)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams

> {%
    client.test("Org admin sees Dev through the org hierarchy", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status was " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.length === 1, "expected 1, got " + response.body.length);
        client.assert(response.body[0].id === client.global.get("teamId"), "should be Dev");
    });
%}

### T9. Fran views the single team → 200
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams/{{teamId}}

> {% client.test("Org admin views the team", function () { client.assert(response.status === 200, "got " + response.status); }); %}

### T10. Fran views Dev members → 200 (org admin ⇒ manage)
GET {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members

> {% client.test("Org admin views members", function () { client.assert(response.status === 200, "got " + response.status); }); %}

### ── As Adam (TEAM admin of Dev) ─────────────────────────────────────

### T11. Login as Adam
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{adamEmail}}&password={{pwd}}&tenant={{slug}}

### T12. Adam lists teams → sees Dev (admin ⇒ view) (1)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams

> {%
    client.test("Team admin sees Dev", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status was " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.length === 1, "expected 1, got " + response.body.length);
    });
%}

### T13. Adam adds Otto as member → 201  ← team admin CAN add members
POST {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamId": "{{teamId}}", "userId": "{{ottoId}}" }

> {% client.test("Team admin adds a member", function () { client.assert(response.status === 201, "expected 201, got " + response.status); }); %}

### T14. Adam views Dev members → 200 (team admin ⇒ manage)
GET {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members

> {% client.test("Team admin views members", function () { client.assert(response.status === 200, "got " + response.status); }); %}

### T15. Adam tries to promote Otto to admin → 403  ← only ORG admin may promote
PUT {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members/{{ottoId}}/admin

> {% client.test("Team admin CANNOT promote", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### T16. Adam tries to create another team → 403 (team admin is not org admin)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/teams
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sales Team" }

> {% client.test("Team admin CANNOT create teams", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### ── As Otto (plain member of Dev) ───────────────────────────────────

### T17. Login as Otto
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{ottoEmail}}&password={{pwd}}&tenant={{slug}}

### T18. Otto views Dev → 200 (member ⇒ view)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams/{{teamId}}

> {% client.test("Member views Dev", function () { client.assert(response.status === 200, "got " + response.status); }); %}

### T19. Otto lists teams → sees Dev (1)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/teams

> {%
    client.test("Member sees Dev", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status was " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.length === 1, "expected 1, got " + response.body.length);
    });
%}

### T20. Otto tries to view the members list → 403 (list needs manage)
GET {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members

> {% client.test("Member CANNOT view the members list", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### T21. Otto tries to add a member → 403 (member has no manage)
POST {{host}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/members
Content-Type: application/json

{ "teamId": "{{teamId}}", "userId": "{{adamId}}" }

> {% client.test("Member CANNOT add members", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### T22. Otto tries to delete the team → 403 (member ≠ manage)
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/teams/{{teamId}}

> {% client.test("Member CANNOT delete the team", function () { client.assert(response.status === 403, "expected 403, got " + response.status); }); %}

### ── Teardown (only org admin may delete the org) ────────────────────

### T23. Login as Fran (org admin)
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

email={{franEmail}}&password={{pwd}}&tenant={{slug}}

### T24. Fran deletes the org → 204. Cascades: Dev team + all tuples removed.
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/organizations/{{orgId}}

> {% client.test("Org admin deletes the org", function () { client.assert(response.status === 204, "expected 204, got " + response.status); }); %}
